===== Installation =====================================

Installation
------------

Copy all files from the release disk into a new directory (eg. KITHKIN)
on your hard disk.

Run KITHKIN.EXE from the File Manager or create a new program item in
the Program Manager and double click on the Kith and Kin icon. You can
launch Kith and Kin from a Tree File (.TRE) if you have associated .TRE
files with KITHKIN.EXE in the File Manager. The program (.EXE), help
(.HLP) and options (.OPT) files must all reside in the same directory.

To get you off to a flying start using Kith and Kin, read the help topic
"Getting Started". This will lead you through the basics.

The file BWCC.DLL should reside in either the KITHKIN or WINDOWS\SYSTEM
directories or in another directory in your PATH. Since it is a common
DLL you may already have it on your system in which case you need only
one copy available.


